Keep a shared numbers as an empty list of whole numbers.
Place 2 into numbers.
Place -1 into numbers.
Place 1 into numbers.
Place 2 into numbers.
Place 2 into numbers.
Keep a shared found as 0.
To seek from start (a whole number) with cap (a whole number).
The direction is item start of numbers.
The current is start.
The next is 0.
The steps is 0.
Repeat while steps is less than cap.
The move is item current of numbers.
The samedir is 1.
If direction is more than 0 and move is less than 0, set samedir to 0.
If direction is less than 0 and move is more than 0, set samedir to 0.
If samedir is 0, set steps to cap.
If samedir is 1, set next to current plus move.
If samedir is 1 and next is less than 0, add cap to next.
If samedir is 1 and next is at least cap, subtract cap from next.
If samedir is 1 and next is current, set steps to cap.
If samedir is 1 and next is start and steps is more than 0, set found to 1, set steps to cap.
If samedir is 1 and next is not current and next is not start, set current to next, add 1 to steps.

The last is the last position of numbers.
The cap is last plus 1.
For every start from 0 to last.
Seek from start with cap.

If found is 1, show true, otherwise show false.
